  "body": "We have a [Chromium bug](https://crbug.com/856269) that asks for the ability to show/hide virtual keyboards on touch devices.  The primary use-case is online editors like Google Docs.\r\n\r\nModifying [the `inputmode` attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#input-modalities:-the-inputmode-attribute) dynamically from/to the \"none\" value could be a possible way to do this.  It turns out that different browsers respond differently to such dynamic changes:\r\n- Chrome on Android detects dynamic changes only when the keyboard is already visible.  So it is possible to hide a already-visible keyboard (by switching to `inputmode=\"none\"`) but not vice versa.\r\n- Safari does not respond to any dynamic change in `inputmode` until the input box is manually refocused.\r\n- Firefox doesn't seem to support the attribute.\r\n\r\nHere is a repro to test this: https://codepen.io/mustaqahmed/full/gOYxLaL\r\n\r\nCan we possibly spec the dynamic change behavior of `inputmode` to support this use-case?",
